            <ArticleTitle>Spinal canal stenosis at the level of axis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1021-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a rare case of marked segmental stenosis of the axis secondary to developmental hypertrophy of the posterior neural arch causing severe neck pain and headache in the occipital region. The patient made a remarkable recovery following decompressive laminectomy and foraminal decompression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
